    "tolerance": null,
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Special value involved is NaN: float array containing NaN passed to pd.array with an integer dtype (dtype='i8' in issue example) silently produced [-9223372036854775808, 1] instead of raising.",
      "Correct handling per passages: raise pd.errors.IntCastingNaNError with message 'Cannot convert non-finite values' rather than silently casting NaN to an integer.",
      "Entry point: NumpyExtensionArray._from_sequence in pandas/core/arrays/numpy_.py; the fix validates NaN via astype_float_to_int_nansafe (renamed from _astype_float_to_int_nansafe in pandas/core/dtypes/astype.py) when dtype.kind is 'i' or 'u' and the asarray result is floating.",
      "Parametrized test test_pd_array_float_with_nan_to_integer_raises covers dtypes i8, int64, u8, uint64 with input np.array([np.nan, 1.0]).",
      "Issue clarification: the issue is about numpy integer dtypes.",
      "No mention of +/-inf, signed zero, or subnormals in the passages."
